  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Breeze-Block Screen",
    "overview": "HifzFlow is built from 1960s Malaysian mosque modernism: a terrazzo floor, a roof of teal mosaic with a folded-plate edge, and perforated concrete breeze-block screens that let light through. The whole mushaf is one such screen. Each of the 604 pages is one block, and a memorised page lets light through its quatrefoil opening. The brand mark is a single block with brass sunlight behind it, so the logo, the tracking grid and the landing screen are the same unit at different sizes.\n\nStructure stays in cool terrazzo neutrals (green-grey, never cream) and teal-black ink. Teal is the committed brand field: the roof band over every signed-in page, and full-height roof fields on the landing and auth pages. Inside a roof field, text and controls use the night palette, so light-on-teal reads the same in both themes. Depth comes from flat overlapping planes and hairline rules. There are no soft shadows on cards or controls, and no gradients.\n\nDensity is operational: the app is a daily tool used on phones, so the world lives in tokens, the roof, the page grid and the today panel, not in decoration. Display type is Archivo pulled wide, like lettering cast in concrete. Running text stays at normal width.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Terrazzo ground, roof-teal field, turquoise light, brass sun, clay for overdue.",
      "One unit, the breeze block, reused for logo, page grid, legends and the landing screen.",
      "A folded-plate pleat strip as the roof line under the app header and over the landing field.",
      "Sharp corners (2px), hairline borders, flat planes, no card or control shadows.",
      "Archivo at two widths: expanded (118%) for display, normal for UI and reading.",
      "Tabular figures on every number that counts pages, days or ayahs."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Light-Through Rule",
        "body": "Turquoise and teal light inside a block means memorised. Never use the density ramp or `state-memorised` for decoration. A lit block is a claim about the user's hifz.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Status Source Rule",
        "body": "Status colours come only from the `state-*` and `hifz-*` tokens. A page never invents its own status colour.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Roof Inverts Rule",
        "body": "Anything placed on a roof field is wrapped in the dark palette, so its text is light on teal in both themes.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Widths Rule",
        "body": "Expanded width only with `font-display`. Body, buttons, labels and form text stay at normal width.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Steady Numbers Rule",
        "body": "Every page count, streak, ayah count and table cell uses tabular figures so readouts never jitter as they increment.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Planes Rule",
        "body": "Surfaces at rest have no shadow. Separate planes with a hairline or a change of tone. A shadow is allowed only on a layer that floats over the page.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do build page-level visuals from the breeze block. One block equals one page.",
      "Do keep text on any roof field in the dark palette (wrap the field in `.dark`).",
      "Do use `font-display` (expanded Archivo) for headings and numerals only.",
      "Do use tabular figures on every count, page number and table cell.",
      "Do take status colours only from `state-*` and `hifz-*` tokens.",
      "Do separate surfaces with 1px hairlines and tone, and keep corners at 2px.",
      "Do honour reduced motion: page enter is 180ms ease-out, and looping motion stops."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use cream or warm-white grounds. Terrazzo is cool green-grey.",
      "Don't add shadows to cards, buttons or inputs, and don't use gradients for fills.",
      "Don't draw more than one pleated roof line in a view.",
      "Don't light a block (turquoise, teal or brass in its opening) unless it states real memorisation data. On marketing surfaces, label example data as an example.",
      "Don't use the Arabic face or sacred text as ornament. Arabic appears only as content, right to left, at line-height 2.1."
    ]
  }
